{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady","id":1489717,"title":"Gift for an ancient vampire lady","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-10T22:14:47-07:00","id":1489717,"title":"Gift for an ancient vampire lady","content":"The year is 1230 and you are good friends with a politically savvy, charismatic, vampire lady who was alive (not yet a vampire) during the 300s and is in love with (and married to) her sire, a slighlty older and somewhat idealistic English (formerly Roman) Ventrue vampire lord. They've founded an influential line of ghouls and are using these to rule one of the richer, more poweful (fictional) county's in England at this time. The family is liked by most of its people.<br /> <br /> You are some sort of fairy wizard lady and want to give her a magic item as a gift.<br /> <br /> What sorts of magical things might a woman like that want?<br /> <br /> (The sire and her family are already getting gifts and so this is for her)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 08-11-2022, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T01:07:54-07:00","id":1489721,"title":"","content":"If it's a magical gift and you want to keep the traditional moral ambiguity of the fairies it could be something that allows the vampire to relive her mortality as a gift ... and as a curse.<br /> Which could make her extremely happy but also obsessed with that gift, opening up to possible new plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T18:29:40-07:00","id":1489822,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting. But what sort of thing would that be.... Maybe something that restores the look, feel, and joys of life?<br /> Edit: like a pendant that makes you seem alive (seem to breathe, have a heartbeat, etc.) and able to partake of mortal pleasures. <br /> What else would be nice, I wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 08-11-2022, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T19:12:42-07:00","id":1489824,"title":"","content":"I read the title in the voice the Adventure Time narrator uses when singing about Marceline in her intro episode. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/AcY7J6K9UEM?t=41\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/AcY7J6K9UEM?t=41\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/AcY7J6K9UEM?t=41\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/AcY7J6K9UEM?t=41 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 08-11-2022, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T01:12:11-07:00","id":1489855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489822#post1489822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds interesting. But what sort of thing would that be.... Maybe something that restores the look, feel, and joys of life?<br /> Edit: like a pendant that makes you seem alive (seem to breathe, have a heartbeat, etc.) and able to partake of mortal pleasures.<br /> What else would be nice, I wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would limit myself to the sensations. She could perceive life as if it were human again, smell and taste, apparently &quot;small&quot; things that give the vampire an idea of what she was missing. And that she begins to obsess her.<br /> <br /> To give you a similar example, ashamed as I am, she thinks of the mirror that showed Harry Potter's dead parents.<br /> <br /> However it must be a sincere gift but inadvertently poisoned by the very nature of the Fairies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T01:56:24-07:00","id":1489860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489855#post1489855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give you a similar example, ashamed as I am, she thinks of the mirror that showed Harry Potter's dead parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you ashamed of this example? It seems pretty fine.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2078_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2078\" data-vbnamecard=\"2078\">Alucard</a>'s mention of Marceline gave me an idea: an umbrella that gives her the illusion of being under a sunny day. It doesn't affect others or really give her any protection against the sun, but it does make her experience the night as if it was day, with all the light and beauty it can bring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T02:44:15-07:00","id":1489863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489860#post1489860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you ashamed of this example? It seems pretty fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am ashamed not to find another equally immediate example.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2078_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2078\" data-vbnamecard=\"2078\">Alucard</a>'s mention of Marceline gave me an idea: an umbrella that gives her the illusion of being under a sunny day. It doesn't affect others or really give her any protection against the sun, but it does make her experience the night as if it was day, with all the light and beauty it can bring. </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","user":"Querion","date":". 08-12-2022, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T08:46:11-07:00","id":1489886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489860#post1489860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you ashamed of this example? It seems pretty fine.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s mention of Marceline gave me an idea: an umbrella that gives her the illusion of being under a sunny day. It doesn't affect others or really give her any protection against the sun, but it does make her experience the night as if it was day, with all the light and beauty it can bring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure she will like that one when she must start to roll fear frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T08:50:24-07:00","id":1489887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489886#post1489886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure she will like that one when she must start to roll fear frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Maybe not. I don't know her or if it will happen, it's a fairy gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T19:30:13-07:00","id":1490209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489855#post1489855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However it must be a sincere gift but inadvertently poisoned by the very nature of the Fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with that. My character has a talent for making magic items that tend to not go exactly as planned even if all the grafting goes perfectly.<br /> <br /> For example; the sword being made for this woman's spouse is a mighty sword made from the guy's blood which will take about 7 to 15 years to make and regular infusions of a few hundred human's worth of that guys blood and in the end, it will arrive at a sword that can grant its wielder some of that vampir'es powers (It's meant for his knight champion) at the cost of attacking its user if they attack people the sword doesn't want them attacking, not being able to put it down until it's full with the blood of the &quot;unjust&quot; or the wielder's blood; and potentially going on some sort of mad &quot;justice crusade&quot; for a few days when they use the powers it grants that they have no chance of learning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T19:32:28-07:00","id":1490210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489860#post1489860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2078_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2078\" data-vbnamecard=\"2078\">Alucard</a>'s mention of Marceline gave me an idea: an umbrella that gives her the illusion of being under a sunny day. It doesn't affect others or really give her any protection against the sun, but it does make her experience the night as if it was day, with all the light and beauty it can bring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually pretty awesome. I'll see if I can make that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T19:37:23-07:00","id":1490211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1489886#post1489886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure she will like that one when she must start to roll fear frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm thinking, what if it comes with a sense of peace that makes the sun in general feel harmless to the beast<br /> <br /> Which makes the beast fine with its effects and not react as strongly to sunlight... until she gets hit by real sunlight, and then the beast overreacts and, for a while, she has a chance to frenzy in the presence of the umbrella and any rendition of the sun. <br /> <br /> (Maybe I shouldn't make this thing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T07:07:25-07:00","id":1490255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489717-gift-for-an-ancient-vampire-lady?p=1490211#post1490211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking, what if it comes with a sense of peace that makes the sun in general feel harmless to the beast<br /> <br /> Which makes the beast fine with its effects and not react as strongly to sunlight... until she gets hit by real sunlight, and then the beast overreacts and, for a while, she has a chance to frenzy in the presence of the umbrella and any rendition of the sun.<br /> <br /> (Maybe I shouldn't make this thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Umbrella may simply protect her from fear of the illusion.<br /> <br /> By the way, mechanically speaking, what <b>exactly</b> your character is? That will make things much easier in terms of giving ideas and evaluating possible effects or how to circumvent them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}